  "result": "Fixed. Options in `--help` now list their short name first again (`-h, --help`, `-v, --verbose`) instead of `--help, -h`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`src/click/formatting.py:319`**: removed `reverse=True` from the sort in `join_options`. Names are now ordered shortest prefix first, and names with the same prefix keep the order they were declared in.\n- **`tests/test_formatting.py`**: added tests that check `join_options` directly and check the end-to-end `--help` output (`-v, --verbose`).\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: version 8.5.0 is already released, so I started a new \"8.5.1 \u2014 Unreleased\" section for the entry.\n\n**Tests:** the full suite passes (1910 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed), including the 4 new tests. I tried to confirm the new tests fail without the fix, but that check didn't work: stashing the changes also removed the new tests, so nothing ran.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
